# Docker sends the entire build context to the daemon before it does anything.
#
# Without this it sends `target/` — 46 GB on a warm workspace — on every `make dev-up`, because the
# `toold` service builds with the repository root as its context. That turned a three-second
# command into minutes of "transferring context" and looked exactly like Docker hanging.
#
# Nothing excluded here is needed inside an image: the Rust build happens in the builder stage from
# source, and the frontend is not containerised in development.

target/
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
.git/
.github/

# Data and generated output. Large, reproducible, and never wanted in an image.
data/raw/
models/
tests/fixtures/corpus/
eval/reports/
*.gguf

# Local state and secrets.
.env
.env.*
*.log
